cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this survey or its companion artifact, please cite it as below."
title: "Multi-Hop Retrieval-Augmented Generation: A Survey of Evidence Dependency, Process Organization, Knowledge Access, and Evaluation Alignment"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Luo
    given-names: Yuqing
    affiliation: University of Science and Technology of China
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Kai
    affiliation: University of Science and Technology of China
  - family-names: He
    given-names: Liyang
    affiliation: University of Science and Technology of China
year: 2026
abstract: >-
  A survey of multi-hop retrieval-augmented generation organized around four
  connected layers: evidence dependency, established retrieval-reasoning
  process organization, external knowledge-access conditions, and evaluation
  alignment. The current structured evidence map contains 274 canonical papers.
  Corpus-level percentages are interpreted as descriptive evidence-backed
  mappings; targeted primary-source rechecking supports the evaluation analysis
  of state-dependent access decisions.
keywords:
  - multi-hop RAG
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - multi-hop question answering
  - evidence dependency
  - retrieval reasoning
  - knowledge access
  - evaluation alignment
  - agentic retrieval
license: MIT
notes: >-
  Author manuscript draft targeting ACM Transactions on Information Systems.
  Review cutoff: 2026-08-05. The broader fine-grained coding scheme did not pass
  the pre-specified confirmatory reliability gate; current corpus percentages
  are descriptive mappings rather than reliability-validated prevalence
  estimates. Add repository DOI and final publisher metadata only after they
  are assigned.
